WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.158
We introduce Audio-R1, reinforcement learning
that helps audio-language models listen and

00:05.158 --> 00:07.245
reason, using puzzles like this one.

00:07.533 --> 00:14.431
[♪ three pieces, shuffled]

00:14.433 --> 00:17.296
Three pieces of one recording, shuffled.

00:17.296 --> 00:18.799
Which order is right?

00:20.283 --> 00:21.630
Two, one, three.

00:21.917 --> 00:27.795
[♪ the original order]

00:27.800 --> 00:35.739
Before our training, Qwen2.5-Omni solves
puzzles like this just 27 percent of the time.

00:35.739 --> 00:38.203
After Audio-R1, 60 percent.

00:39.300 --> 00:42.737
We make these puzzles by
cutting and shuffling raw audio,

00:42.737 --> 00:45.208
so every answer is known by construction:

00:45.208 --> 00:46.173
no human labels.

00:46.467 --> 00:48.407
The model reasons, then answers.

00:48.407 --> 00:52.835
A simple rule checks the answer, plus
a small bonus for the right format,

00:52.835 --> 00:54.594
and that check is the reward.

00:54.883 --> 00:59.156
Eight answers per puzzle; GRPO favors
those above the group average.

01:00.250 --> 01:02.637
Besides ordering, there's Region Inpainting:

01:02.637 --> 01:07.030
it silences the middle of a clip and asks
which of four candidates fills the gap.

01:07.317 --> 01:11.450
Identity Detection asks which candidates
are the same recording as an anchor.

01:12.533 --> 01:18.756
On Qwen2.5-Omni, each puzzle helps on its
own, and all three together work best.

01:19.050 --> 01:21.366
Same puzzles, supervised fine-tuning:

01:21.366 --> 01:24.996
it learns them about as well,
but transfers only modestly.

01:24.996 --> 01:27.688
Reinforcement learning transfers much more.

01:29.083 --> 01:32.495
An LLM-based judge model scored
the traces, given the audio,

01:32.495 --> 01:34.656
the question and the reference answer.

01:34.950 --> 01:39.130
It scores completeness, logical
coherence, and audio groundedness.

01:39.417 --> 01:44.321
Audio-R1 outperforms base and SFT
consistently on all three scores.

01:44.321 --> 01:47.761
Fine-tuning mostly scores below the base model:

01:47.761 --> 01:50.469
imitating answers can hurt reasoning.

01:51.567 --> 01:56.443
On four audio-language models, Audio-R1
improved every benchmark we tested.

01:56.733 --> 02:01.331
With Qwen3-Omni, it reaches the highest
scores of all the models we compared.

02:01.617 --> 02:02.661
Want to learn more?

02:02.661 --> 02:04.914
Visit our project page at the link below.
